course: dictionary
lesson: 16148
title: Wince: a quick face of pain
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To wince is to make a quick face or a small movement when you feel pain, or when you see or hear something unpleasant. You may not say a word, but your face tells everyone. «She winced when the cold water touched her cut.» The cold water stung, so wince means a quick face of pain.
explain: A wince is quick. It is over in a flash, unlike a long cry. «He gave a wince when he sat on the sharp stone.» Here wince is a noun, a thing he gave. In «He winced when he sat down», it is a verb, something he did. Ask yourself: is it an action or a thing?
explain: Wince can also show embarrassment, when something is awkward rather than painful. «I winced when my name was called out wrongly in assembly.» Nobody hurt me, but my face showed I felt uncomfortable. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "I made a quick face because of it" still makes sense.
fact: To wince means to make a quick face or small movement when you feel pain or see or hear something unpleasant.
fact: A wince is that quick look of pain. It can be a verb («she winced») or a noun («with a wince»).
fact: Verb forms: wince, winces, winced, wincing.
fact: «Make someone wince» means to make someone feel pain or discomfort, so they pull a face.
fact: «Wince in pain» is a common phrase: the face shows the hurt before any words come out.
exercise: «She winced as the nurse cleaned the cut.» What does winced mean here? | Ran out of the room | Fell fast asleep | *Made a quick face of pain | Laughed loudly at the nurse
exercise: «He gave a wince when he sat on the sharp stone.» Is wince a verb or a noun in this sentence? | A verb, to sleep | A noun, a loud shout | A verb, to run very fast | *A noun, a quick look of pain
exercise: Find and copy the word that shows a quick face of pain in «With a wince, Sam lifted the heavy box.» | box | *wince | lifted | Sam
test: «The screech of chalk on the board made everyone wince.» What does made everyone wince mean? | *Made everyone pull a quick, uncomfortable face | Made everyone sleepy | Made everyone laugh and clap | Made everyone stand up and cheer
test: Which word fits the gap? «Yesterday she ___ when the door slammed on her finger.» | smiled | ran | *winced | cry
exam: Which sentence uses wince correctly? | *She winced when she bit into the sour lemon. | The cake winced in the oven. | The bus winced slowly down the road. | He winced with joy when he won the prize.
